IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa18-part23-ch1`

-- coa18-part23-ch3.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 23 (distributions), Chapter 3 (supplementary
-- provisions), ss 841 to 853: realised losses and profits, distributions in kind, the consequences of an unlawful
-- distribution, the savings and the minor definitions. Lines 11304-11425 of ukpga-2006-46.txt. Layer 1: the law, objectively.
-- How to read an answer (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, NOTHING) is as in the header of coa18-part22-notice.l4. It imports
-- coa18-part23-ch1 for the type `s 831(3) kind of relevant accounts`.
--
-- SEAMS (inputs): `s 396 ...` (provisions and notes specified by regulations), `s 1163(1) the asset is a non-cash asset`
-- (BOOLEAN), `s 1165(2) the company is an authorised insurance company` (BOOLEAN), `s 678`/`s 679` (Part 18).
-- ANSWERS OTHER PARTS ASK FOR (PLAN section 6): `s 853(2)`, `s 853(3) the operation is capitalisation`, `s 853(4) the profit
-- or loss is a realised profit or loss`, `s 853(6) the asset is a fixed asset`.

§ `Part 23 (ss 829 to 853), Chapter 3: ss 841 to 853`

§§ `s 841 Realised losses and profits and revaluation of fixed assets`

-- src:11311 | (3) A “revaluation provision” means a provision in respect of a diminution in value of a fixed asset appearing on a revaluation of all the fixed assets of the company, or of all of its fixed assets other than goodwill.
@ref s 841(3) Realised losses and profits and revaluation of fixed assets (src:11311-11311)
GIVEN `the provision is in respect of a diminution in value of a fixed asset` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the diminution appears on a revaluation of all the fixed assets of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the diminution appears on a revaluation of all the fixed assets of the company other than goodwill` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 841(3) the provision is a revaluation provision` MEANS
    IF     `the provision is in respect of a diminution in value of a fixed asset`
       AND (   `the diminution appears on a revaluation of all the fixed assets of the company`
            OR `the diminution appears on a revaluation of all the fixed assets of the company other than goodwill`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A “revaluation provision” means a provision in respect of a diminution in value of a fixed asset appearing on a revaluation of all the fixed assets of the company, or of all of its fixed assets other than goodwill."

-- src:11308 | (2) The following are treated as realised losses—
-- src:11309 | (a) in the case of Companies Act accounts, provisions of a kind specified for the purposes of this paragraph by regulations under section 396 (except revaluation provisions);
-- src:11310 | (b) in the case of IAS accounts, provisions of any kind (except revaluation provisions).
@ref s 841(2) Realised losses and profits and revaluation of fixed assets (src:11308-11310)
GIVEN accounts IS A `s 831(3) kind of relevant accounts`
      `s 396 the provision is of a kind specified for the purposes of section 841(2)(a) by regulations under section 396` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 841(3) the provision is a revaluation provision` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 841(2) the provision is treated as a realised loss` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 841(3) the provision is a revaluation provision` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "provisions of a kind specified ... (except revaluation provisions)" and "provisions of any kind (except revaluation provisions)"
        IF accounts EQUALS `s 831(3)(b) IAS accounts` THEN (IF `s 841(3) the provision is a revaluation provision` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING) -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the provision is a revaluation provision is not known
        IF accounts EQUALS `s 831(3)(a) Companies Act accounts` THEN
            (IF `s 396 the provision is of a kind specified for the purposes of section 841(2)(a) by regulations under section 396` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `s 841(3) the provision is a revaluation provision` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING) -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "provisions of a kind specified for the purposes of this paragraph by regulations under section 396": the kinds are in s 396; "The following are treated as realised losses" does not close the list
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the subsection names Companies Act accounts and IAS accounts only

-- src:11312 | (4) For the purpose of subsections (2) and (3) any consideration by the directors of the value at a particular time of a fixed asset is treated as a revaluation provided—
-- src:11313 | (a) the directors are satisfied that the aggregate value at that time of the fixed assets of the company that have not actually been revalued is not less than the aggregate amount at which they are then stated in the company's accounts, and
-- src:11314 | (b) it is stated in a note to the accounts—
-- src:11315 | (i) that the directors have considered the value of some or all of the fixed assets of the company without actually revaluing them,
-- src:11316 | (ii) that they are satisfied that the aggregate value of those assets at the time of their consideration was not less than the aggregate amount at which they were then stated in the company's accounts, and
-- src:11317 | (iii) that accordingly, by virtue of this subsection, amounts are stated in the accounts on the basis that a revaluation of fixed assets of the company is treated as having taken place at that time.
@ref s 841(4) Realised losses and profits and revaluation of fixed assets (src:11312-11317)
GIVEN `the directors have considered the value at a particular time of a fixed asset` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors are satisfied that the aggregate value at that time of the fixed assets of the company that have not actually been revalued is not less than the aggregate amount at which they are then stated in the company's accounts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a note to the accounts states that the directors have considered the value of some or all of the fixed assets of the company without actually revaluing them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a note to the accounts states that they are satisfied that the aggregate value of those assets at the time of their consideration was not less than the aggregate amount at which they were then stated in the company's accounts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a note to the accounts states that accordingly, by virtue of this subsection, amounts are stated in the accounts on the basis that a revaluation of fixed assets of the company is treated as having taken place at that time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 841(4) the consideration by the directors of the value of a fixed asset is treated as a revaluation` MEANS
    IF     `the directors have considered the value at a particular time of a fixed asset`
       AND `the directors are satisfied that the aggregate value at that time of the fixed assets of the company that have not actually been revalued is not less than the aggregate amount at which they are then stated in the company's accounts`
       AND `a note to the accounts states that the directors have considered the value of some or all of the fixed assets of the company without actually revaluing them`
       AND `a note to the accounts states that they are satisfied that the aggregate value of those assets at the time of their consideration was not less than the aggregate amount at which they were then stated in the company's accounts`
       AND `a note to the accounts states that accordingly, by virtue of this subsection, amounts are stated in the accounts on the basis that a revaluation of fixed assets of the company is treated as having taken place at that time`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any consideration by the directors of the value at a particular time of a fixed asset is treated as a revaluation provided— (a) the directors are satisfied ..., and (b) it is stated in a note to the accounts— (i) ..., (ii) ..., and (iii) ..."

-- src:11318 | (5) Where—
-- src:11319 | (a) on the revaluation of a fixed asset, an unrealised profit is shown to have been made, and
-- src:11320 | (b) on or after the revaluation, a sum is written off or retained for depreciation of that asset over a period,
-- src:11321 | an amount equal to the amount by which that sum exceeds the sum which would have been so written off or retained for the depreciation of that asset over that period, if that profit had not been made, is treated as a realised profit made over that period.
@ref s 841(5) Realised losses and profits and revaluation of fixed assets (src:11318-11321)
GIVEN `on the revaluation of a fixed asset, an unrealised profit is shown to have been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `on or after the revaluation, a sum is written off or retained for depreciation of that asset over a period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sum written off or retained for depreciation over that period` IS A NUMBER
      `the sum which would have been so written off or retained for the depreciation of that asset over that period if that profit had not been made` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 841(5) the amount treated as a realised profit made over that period` MEANS
    IF `on the revaluation of a fixed asset, an unrealised profit is shown to have been made` AND `on or after the revaluation, a sum is written off or retained for depreciation of that asset over a period`
    THEN JUST (IF `the sum written off or retained for depreciation over that period` GREATER THAN `the sum which would have been so written off or retained for the depreciation of that asset over that period if that profit had not been made` THEN `the sum written off or retained for depreciation over that period` MINUS `the sum which would have been so written off or retained for the depreciation of that asset over that period if that profit had not been made` ELSE 0)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where— (a) on the revaluation of a fixed asset, an unrealised profit is shown to have been made, and (b) on or after the revaluation, a sum is written off or retained for depreciation of that asset over a period": the number is not defined elsewhere

§§ `s 842 Determination of profit or loss in respect of asset where records incomplete`

-- src:11323 | In determining for the purposes of this Part whether a company has made a profit or loss in respect of an asset where—
-- src:11324 | (a) there is no record of the original cost of the asset, or
-- src:11325 | (b) a record cannot be obtained without unreasonable expense or delay,
-- src:11326 | its cost is taken to be the value ascribed to it in the earliest available record of its value made on or after its acquisition by the company.
@ref s 842 Determination of profit or loss in respect of asset where records incomplete (src:11323-11326)
GIVEN `there is no record of the original cost of the asset` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a record cannot be obtained without unreasonable expense or delay` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the value ascribed to the asset in the earliest available record of its value made on or after its acquisition by the company` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 842 the cost of the asset taken for the purposes of determining profit or loss` MEANS
    IF `there is no record of the original cost of the asset` OR `a record cannot be obtained without unreasonable expense or delay`
    THEN JUST `the value ascribed to the asset in the earliest available record of its value made on or after its acquisition by the company`
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In determining ... whether a company has made a profit or loss in respect of an asset where— (a) there is no record of the original cost of the asset, or (b) a record cannot be obtained without unreasonable expense or delay": the cost in other cases is not given by this section

§§ `s 843 Realised profits and losses of long-term insurance business of certain insurance companies`

-- src:11328 | (1) The provisions of this section have effect for the purposes of this Part as it applies in relation to an authorised insurance company carrying on long-term business, other than—
-- src:11329 | (a) a person to whom section 833A applies; or
-- src:11330 | (b) an insurance special purpose vehicle.
@ref s 843(1) Realised profits and losses of long-term insurance business of certain insurance companies (src:11328-11330)
GIVEN `s 1165(2) the company is an authorised insurance company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company carries on long-term business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 833A applies to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is an insurance special purpose vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 843(1) the provisions of this section have effect in relation to the company` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `s 1165(2) the company is an authorised insurance company`) OR (NOT `the company carries on long-term business`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "as it applies in relation to an authorised insurance company carrying on long-term business"
        IF `section 833A applies to the company` OR `the company is an insurance special purpose vehicle` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "other than— (a) a person to whom section 833A applies; or (b) an insurance special purpose vehicle" (an (other than X) site: fork register)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:11331 | (2) An amount included in the relevant part of the company's balance sheet that—
-- src:11332 | (a) represents a surplus in the fund or funds maintained by it in respect of its long-term business, and
-- src:11333 | (b) has not been allocated to policy holders or, as the case may be, carried forward unappropriated in accordance with asset identification rules made under Part 9A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (c. 8),
-- src:11334 | is treated as a realised profit.
@ref s 843(2) Realised profits and losses of long-term insurance business of certain insurance companies (src:11331-11334)
GIVEN `the amount is included in the relevant part of the company's balance sheet` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount represents a surplus in the fund or funds maintained by the company in respect of its long-term business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount has not been allocated to policy holders or carried forward unappropriated in accordance with asset identification rules made under Part 9A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 843(2) the amount is treated as a realised profit` MEANS
    IF     `the amount is included in the relevant part of the company's balance sheet`
       AND `the amount represents a surplus in the fund or funds maintained by the company in respect of its long-term business`
       AND `the amount has not been allocated to policy holders or carried forward unappropriated in accordance with asset identification rules made under Part 9A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An amount included in the relevant part of the company's balance sheet that— (a) represents a surplus ..., and (b) has not been allocated ... is treated as a realised profit"

-- src:11335 | (3) For the purposes of subsection (2)—
-- src:11336 | (a) the relevant part of the balance sheet is that part of the balance sheet that represents accumulated profit or loss;
-- src:11337 | (b) a surplus in the fund or funds maintained by the company in respect of its long-term business means an excess of the assets representing that fund or those funds over the liabilities of the company attributable to its long-term business, as shown by an actuarial investigation.
@ref s 843(3) Realised profits and losses of long-term insurance business of certain insurance companies (src:11335-11337)
GIVEN `the part of the balance sheet represents accumulated profit or loss` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 843(3)(a) the part of the balance sheet is the relevant part` MEANS
    IF `the part of the balance sheet represents accumulated profit or loss`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the relevant part of the balance sheet is that part of the balance sheet that represents accumulated profit or loss"

@ref s 843(3)(b) Realised profits and losses of long-term insurance business of certain insurance companies (src:11337-11337)
GIVEN `the assets representing the fund or funds, as shown by an actuarial investigation` IS A NUMBER
      `the liabilities of the company attributable to its long-term business, as shown by an actuarial investigation` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 843(3)(b) the surplus in the fund or funds maintained by the company in respect of its long-term business` MEANS
    IF `the assets representing the fund or funds, as shown by an actuarial investigation` GREATER THAN `the liabilities of the company attributable to its long-term business, as shown by an actuarial investigation`
    THEN `the assets representing the fund or funds, as shown by an actuarial investigation` MINUS `the liabilities of the company attributable to its long-term business, as shown by an actuarial investigation`
    ELSE 0

-- src:11338 | (4) A deficit in the fund or funds maintained by the company in respect of its long-term business is treated as a realised loss.
-- src:11339 | For this purpose a deficit in any such fund or funds means an excess of the liabilities of the company attributable to its long-term business over the assets representing that fund or those funds, as shown by an actuarial investigation.
@ref s 843(4) Realised profits and losses of long-term insurance business of certain insurance companies (src:11338-11339)
GIVEN `the liabilities of the company attributable to its long-term business, as shown by an actuarial investigation` IS A NUMBER
      `the assets representing the fund or funds, as shown by an actuarial investigation` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 843(4) the deficit in the fund or funds maintained by the company in respect of its long-term business, treated as a realised loss` MEANS
    IF `the liabilities of the company attributable to its long-term business, as shown by an actuarial investigation` GREATER THAN `the assets representing the fund or funds, as shown by an actuarial investigation`
    THEN `the liabilities of the company attributable to its long-term business, as shown by an actuarial investigation` MINUS `the assets representing the fund or funds, as shown by an actuarial investigation`
    ELSE 0

-- src:11340 | (5) Subject to subsections (2) and (4), any profit or loss arising in the company's long-term business is to be left out of account.
@ref s 843(5) Realised profits and losses of long-term insurance business of certain insurance companies (src:11340-11340)
GIVEN `the profit or loss arises in the company's long-term business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount is treated under subsection (2) or (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 843(5) the profit or loss is left out of account` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the profit or loss arises in the company's long-term business`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any profit or loss arising in the company's long-term business is to be left out of account"
        IF `the amount is treated under subsection (2) or (4)` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to subsections (2) and (4), any profit or loss arising in the company's long-term business is to be left out of account." (a "subject to" met)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:11341 | (6) For the purposes of this section an “actuarial investigation” means an investigation made into the financial condition of an authorised insurance company in respect of its long-term business—
-- src:11342 | (a) carried out once in every period of twelve months in accordance with rules made under Part 9A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000, or
-- src:11343 | (b) carried out in accordance with a requirement imposed under section 166 of that Act,
-- src:11344 | by an actuary appointed as actuary to the company.
@ref s 843(6) Realised profits and losses of long-term insurance business of certain insurance companies (src:11341-11344)
GIVEN `the investigation is made into the financial condition of an authorised insurance company in respect of its long-term business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the investigation is carried out once in every period of twelve months in accordance with rules made under Part 9A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the investigation is carried out in accordance with a requirement imposed under section 166 of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the investigation is made by an actuary appointed as actuary to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 843(6) the investigation is an actuarial investigation` MEANS
    IF     `the investigation is made into the financial condition of an authorised insurance company in respect of its long-term business`
       AND (   `the investigation is carried out once in every period of twelve months in accordance with rules made under Part 9A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000`
            OR `the investigation is carried out in accordance with a requirement imposed under section 166 of that Act`)
       AND `the investigation is made by an actuary appointed as actuary to the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an “actuarial investigation” means an investigation made into the financial condition of an authorised insurance company in respect of its long-term business— (a) carried out once in every period of twelve months ..., or (b) carried out in accordance with a requirement imposed under section 166 of that Act, by an actuary appointed as actuary to the company"

-- src:11345 | (7) In this section “long-term business” means business that consists of effecting or carrying out contracts of long-term insurance.
-- src:11346 | This definition must be read with section 22 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000, any relevant order under that section and Schedule 2 to that Act.
@ref s 843(7) Realised profits and losses of long-term insurance business of certain insurance companies (src:11345-11346)
GIVEN `the business consists of effecting or carrying out contracts of long-term insurance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 843(7) the business is long-term business` MEANS
    IF `the business consists of effecting or carrying out contracts of long-term insurance`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In this section “long-term business” means business that consists of effecting or carrying out contracts of long-term insurance." (read with s 22 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000, outside the sources)

-- src:11347 | (8) In this section “ insurance special purpose vehicle ” means a special purpose vehicle within the meaning of Article 13(26) of Directive 2009/138/EC of the European Parliament and of the Council of 25 November 2009 on the taking-up and pursuit of the business of Insurance and Reinsurance (Solvency II) .
@ref s 843(8) Realised profits and losses of long-term insurance business of certain insurance companies (src:11347-11347)
GIVEN `the vehicle is a special purpose vehicle within the meaning of Article 13(26) of Directive 2009/138/EC of the European Parliament and of the Council of 25 November 2009 on the taking-up and pursuit of the business of Insurance and Reinsurance (Solvency II)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 843(8) the vehicle is an insurance special purpose vehicle` MEANS
    IF `the vehicle is a special purpose vehicle within the meaning of Article 13(26) of Directive 2009/138/EC of the European Parliament and of the Council of 25 November 2009 on the taking-up and pursuit of the business of Insurance and Reinsurance (Solvency II)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In this section “ insurance special purpose vehicle ” means a special purpose vehicle within the meaning of Article 13(26) of Directive 2009/138/EC"

§§ `s 844 Treatment of development costs`

-- (2) and (3) are the exceptions; (1) takes their answers as inputs.
-- src:11353 | (2) Subsection (1) does not apply to any part of that amount representing an unrealised profit made on revaluation of those costs.
@ref s 844(2) Treatment of development costs (src:11353-11353)
GIVEN `the part of the amount represents an unrealised profit made on revaluation of those costs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 844(2) subsection (1) does not apply to the part of the amount` MEANS
    IF `the part of the amount represents an unrealised profit made on revaluation of those costs`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subsection (1) does not apply to any part of that amount representing an unrealised profit made on revaluation of those costs."

-- src:11354 | (3) Subsection (1) does not apply if—
-- src:11355 | (a) there are special circumstances in the company's case justifying the directors in deciding that the amount there mentioned is not to be treated as required by subsection (1),
-- src:11356 | (b) it is stated—
-- src:11357 | (i) in the case of Companies Act accounts, in the note required by regulations under section 396 as to the reasons for showing development costs as an asset, or
-- src:11358 | (ii) in the case of IAS accounts, in any note to the accounts,
-- src:11359 | that the amount is not to be so treated, and
-- src:11360 | (c) the note explains the circumstances relied upon to justify the decision of the directors to that effect.
@ref s 844(3) Treatment of development costs (src:11354-11360)
GIVEN `there are special circumstances in the company's case justifying the directors in deciding that the amount is not to be treated as required by subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      accounts IS A `s 831(3) kind of relevant accounts`
      `s 396 the statement is made in the note required by regulations under section 396 as to the reasons for showing development costs as an asset` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the statement is made in a note to the accounts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the note states that the amount is not to be so treated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the note explains the circumstances relied upon to justify the decision of the directors to that effect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 844(3) subsection (1) does not apply` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (   `there are special circumstances in the company's case justifying the directors in deciding that the amount is not to be treated as required by subsection (1)`
                AND `the note states that the amount is not to be so treated`
                AND `the note explains the circumstances relied upon to justify the decision of the directors to that effect`))
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not apply if— (a) there are special circumstances ..., (b) it is stated ... that the amount is not to be so treated, and (c) the note explains the circumstances relied upon"
        IF accounts EQUALS `s 831(3)(b) IAS accounts` THEN
            (IF `the statement is made in a note to the accounts` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE) -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(ii) in the case of IAS accounts, in any note to the accounts"
        IF accounts EQUALS `s 831(3)(a) Companies Act accounts` THEN
            (CONSIDER `s 396 the statement is made in the note required by regulations under section 396 as to the reasons for showing development costs as an asset`
             WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
             WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(i) in the case of Companies Act accounts, in the note required by regulations under section 396 as to the reasons for showing development costs as an asset"
             OTHERWISE NOTHING) -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): which note regulations under s 396 require is outside this Part
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the paragraph names Companies Act accounts and IAS accounts only

-- src:11349 | (1) Where development costs are shown or included as an asset in a company's accounts, any amount shown or included in respect of those costs is treated—
-- src:11350 | (a) for the purposes of section 830 (distributions to be made out of profits available for the purpose) as a realised loss, and
-- src:11351 | (b) for the purposes of section 832 (distributions by investment companies out of accumulated revenue profits) as a realised revenue loss.
-- src:11352 | This is subject to the following exceptions.
@ref s 844(1) Treatment of development costs (src:11349-11352)
GIVEN `development costs are shown or included as an asset in the company's accounts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 844(2) subsection (1) does not apply to the part of the amount` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 844(3) subsection (1) does not apply` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 844(1)(a) the amount shown or included in respect of the development costs is treated, for the purposes of section 830, as a realised loss` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `development costs are shown or included as an asset in the company's accounts`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where development costs are shown or included as an asset in a company's accounts, any amount shown or included in respect of those costs is treated"
        IF `s 844(2) subsection (1) does not apply to the part of the amount` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `s 844(3) subsection (1) does not apply` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This is subject to the following exceptions." and "Subsection (1) does not apply ..."
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 844(1)(b) Treatment of development costs (src:11351-11351)
GIVEN `development costs are shown or included as an asset in the company's accounts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 844(2) subsection (1) does not apply to the part of the amount` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 844(3) subsection (1) does not apply` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 844(1)(b) the amount shown or included in respect of the development costs is treated, for the purposes of section 832, as a realised revenue loss` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `development costs are shown or included as an asset in the company's accounts`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where development costs are shown or included as an asset in a company's accounts, any amount shown or included in respect of those costs is treated"
        IF `s 844(2) subsection (1) does not apply to the part of the amount` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `s 844(3) subsection (1) does not apply` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This is subject to the following exceptions." and "Subsection (1) does not apply ..."
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 845 Distributions in kind: determination of amount`

-- src:11363 | (1) This section applies for determining the amount of a distribution consisting of or including, or treated as arising in consequence of, the sale, transfer or other disposition by a company of a non-cash asset where—
-- src:11364 | (a) at the time of the distribution the company has profits available for distribution, and
-- src:11365 | (b) if the amount of the distribution were to be determined in accordance with this section, the company could make the distribution without contravening this Part.
@ref s 845(1) Distributions in kind: determination of amount (src:11363-11365)
GIVEN `s 1163(1) the asset is a non-cash asset` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the distribution consists of or includes, or is treated as arising in consequence of, the sale, transfer or other disposition by the company of the asset` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at the time of the distribution the company has profits available for distribution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `if the amount of the distribution were to be determined in accordance with this section, the company could make the distribution without contravening this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 845(1) this section applies for determining the amount of the distribution` MEANS
    IF     `s 1163(1) the asset is a non-cash asset`
       AND `the distribution consists of or includes, or is treated as arising in consequence of, the sale, transfer or other disposition by the company of the asset`
       AND `at the time of the distribution the company has profits available for distribution`
       AND `if the amount of the distribution were to be determined in accordance with this section, the company could make the distribution without contravening this Part`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies for determining the amount of a distribution consisting of or including, or treated as arising in consequence of, the sale, transfer or other disposition by a company of a non-cash asset where— (a) at the time of the distribution the company has profits available for distribution, and (b) if the amount of the distribution were to be determined in accordance with this section, the company could make the distribution without contravening this Part."

-- src:11370 | (4) In this section “book value”, in relation to an asset, means—
-- src:11371 | (a) the amount at which the asset is stated in the relevant accounts, or
-- src:11372 | (b) where the asset is not stated in those accounts at any amount, zero.
@ref s 845(4) Distributions in kind: determination of amount (src:11370-11372)
GIVEN `the amount at which the asset is stated in the relevant accounts, if it is stated at any amount` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 845(4) the book value of the asset` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the amount at which the asset is stated in the relevant accounts, if it is stated at any amount`
    WHEN JUST amount THEN amount
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 0

-- src:11366 | (2) The amount of the distribution (or the relevant part of it) is taken to be—
-- src:11367 | (a) in a case where the amount or value of the consideration for the disposition is not less than the book value of the asset, zero;
-- src:11368 | (b) in any other case, the amount by which the book value of the asset exceeds the amount or value of any consideration for the disposition.
@ref s 845(2) Distributions in kind: determination of amount (src:11366-11368)
GIVEN `the amount or value of the consideration for the disposition` IS A NUMBER
      `the book value of the asset` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 845(2) the amount of the distribution or the relevant part of it` MEANS
    IF `the amount or value of the consideration for the disposition` AT LEAST `the book value of the asset`
    THEN 0
    ELSE `the book value of the asset` MINUS `the amount or value of the consideration for the disposition`

-- src:11369 | (3) For the purposes of subsection (1)(a) the company's profits available for distribution are treated as increased by the amount (if any) by which the amount or value of any consideration for the disposition exceeds the book value of the asset.
@ref s 845(3) Distributions in kind: determination of amount (src:11369-11369)
GIVEN `the company's profits available for distribution` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount or value of the consideration for the disposition` IS A NUMBER
      `the book value of the asset` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 845(3) the company's profits available for distribution for the purposes of subsection (1)(a)` MEANS
    `the company's profits available for distribution` PLUS (IF `the amount or value of the consideration for the disposition` GREATER THAN `the book value of the asset` THEN `the amount or value of the consideration for the disposition` MINUS `the book value of the asset` ELSE 0)

-- src:11373 | (5) The provisions of Chapter 2 (justification of distribution by reference to accounts) have effect subject to this section.
@ref s 845(5) Distributions in kind: determination of amount (src:11373-11373)
GIVEN `s 845(1) this section applies for determining the amount of the distribution` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 845(5) the provisions of Chapter 2 have effect subject to this section` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 845(1) this section applies for determining the amount of the distribution`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The provisions of Chapter 2 ... have effect subject to this section": only where this section applies

§§ `s 846 Distributions in kind: treatment of unrealised profits`

-- src:11375 | (1) This section applies where—
-- src:11376 | (a) a company makes a distribution consisting of or including, or treated as arising in consequence of, the sale, transfer or other disposition by the company of a non-cash asset, and
-- src:11377 | (b) any part of the amount at which that asset is stated in the relevant accounts represents an unrealised profit.
@ref s 846(1) Distributions in kind: treatment of unrealised profits (src:11375-11377)
GIVEN `the company makes a distribution consisting of or including, or treated as arising in consequence of, the sale, transfer or other disposition by the company of a non-cash asset` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any part of the amount at which that asset is stated in the relevant accounts represents an unrealised profit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 846(1) this section applies` MEANS
    IF `the company makes a distribution consisting of or including, or treated as arising in consequence of, the sale, transfer or other disposition by the company of a non-cash asset` AND `any part of the amount at which that asset is stated in the relevant accounts represents an unrealised profit`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where— (a) a company makes a distribution consisting of or including ... a non-cash asset, and (b) any part of the amount at which that asset is stated in the relevant accounts represents an unrealised profit."

-- src:11378 | (2) That profit is treated as a realised profit—
-- src:11379 | (a) for the purpose of determining the lawfulness of the distribution in accordance with this Part (whether before or after the distribution takes place), and
-- src:11380 | (b) for the purpose of the application, in relation to anything done with a view to or in connection with the making of the distribution, of any provision of regulations under section 396 under which only realised profits are to be included in or transferred to the profit and loss account.
@ref s 846(2) Distributions in kind: treatment of unrealised profits (src:11378-11380)
GIVEN `s 846(1) this section applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 846(2)(a) that profit is treated as a realised profit for the purpose of determining the lawfulness of the distribution` MEANS
    `s 846(1) this section applies` -- JUST TRUE: treated as realised (whether before or after the distribution takes place); JUST FALSE: the section does not apply (marginal reading (a)); NOTHING stays NOTHING

@ref s 846(2)(b) Distributions in kind: treatment of unrealised profits (src:11380-11380)
GIVEN `s 846(1) this section applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 396 a provision of regulations under section 396 provides that only realised profits are to be included in or transferred to the profit and loss account` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 846(2)(b) that profit is treated as a realised profit for the purpose of applying that provision of the regulations` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 846(1) this section applies`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where ..." (subsection (1)) and so subsection (2) does not
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        CONSIDER `s 396 a provision of regulations under section 396 provides that only realised profits are to be included in or transferred to the profit and loss account`
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "any provision of regulations under section 396 under which only realised profits are to be included in or transferred to the profit and loss account": the provision is in the regulations, outside the sources
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether this section applies is not known

§§ `s 847 Consequences of unlawful distribution`

DECLARE `s 847(2) liability of the member` IS ONE OF
    `s 847(2)(a) liable to repay the distribution or that part of it to the company`
    `s 847(2)(b) liable to pay the company a sum equal to the value of the distribution or that part at that time`
    `s 847(2) not liable under this subsection`

-- src:11384 | (2) If at the time of the distribution the member knows or has reasonable grounds for believing that it is so made, he is liable—
-- src:11385 | (a) to repay it (or that part of it, as the case may be) to the company, or
-- src:11386 | (b) in the case of a distribution made otherwise than in cash, to pay the company a sum equal to the value of the distribution (or part) at that time.
@ref s 847(2) Consequences of unlawful distribution (src:11384-11386)
GIVEN `the distribution, or part of one, made by the company to the member is made in contravention of this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at the time of the distribution the member knows or has reasonable grounds for believing that it is so made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the distribution was made in cash` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the distribution is financial assistance given in contravention of section 678 or 679, or a payment in respect of the redemption or purchase by the company of shares in itself` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 847(2) liability of the member`
`s 847(2) what the member is liable to do` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the distribution, or part of one, made by the company to the member is made in contravention of this Part`) THEN `s 847(2) not liable under this subsection` -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where a distribution, or part of one, made by a company to one of its members is made in contravention of this Part."
        IF `the distribution is financial assistance given in contravention of section 678 or 679, or a payment in respect of the redemption or purchase by the company of shares in itself` THEN `s 847(2) not liable under this subsection` -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not apply in relation to— (a) financial assistance given by a company in contravention of section 678 or 679, or (b) any payment made by a company in respect of the redemption or purchase by the company of shares in itself."
        IF (NOT `at the time of the distribution the member knows or has reasonable grounds for believing that it is so made`) THEN `s 847(2) not liable under this subsection` -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If at the time of the distribution the member knows or has reasonable grounds for believing that it is so made, he is liable" (a failed "if": marginal reading (a))
        IF `the distribution was made in cash` THEN `s 847(2)(a) liable to repay the distribution or that part of it to the company`
        OTHERWISE `s 847(2)(b) liable to pay the company a sum equal to the value of the distribution or that part at that time`

-- src:11387 | (3) This is without prejudice to any obligation imposed apart from this section on a member of a company to repay a distribution unlawfully made to him.
@ref s 847(3) Consequences of unlawful distribution (src:11387-11387)
GIVEN `the member is subject to an obligation imposed apart from this section to repay a distribution unlawfully made to him` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 847(3) the obligation imposed apart from this section is unaffected` MEANS
    IF `the member is subject to an obligation imposed apart from this section to repay a distribution unlawfully made to him`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This is without prejudice to any obligation imposed apart from this section on a member of a company to repay a distribution unlawfully made to him."

§§ `s 848 Saving for certain older provisions in articles`

-- src:11394 | (2) For this purpose the relevant date is—
-- src:11395 | (a) for companies registered in Great Britain, 22nd December 1980;
-- src:11396 | (b) for companies registered in Northern Ireland, 1st July 1983.
@ref s 848(2) Saving for certain older provisions in articles (src:11394-11396)
GIVEN `the place where the company is registered` IS A `Place of registration`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 848(2) the relevant date for a company registered in the place` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the place where the company is registered`
    WHEN `England and Wales` THEN Date 22 12 1980
    WHEN `Scotland` THEN Date 22 12 1980
    WHEN `Northern Ireland` THEN Date 1 7 1983

-- src:11393 | (1) Where immediately before the relevant date a company was authorised by a provision of its articles to apply its unrealised profits in paying up in full or in part unissued shares to be allotted to members of the company as fully or partly paid bonus shares, that provision continues (subject to any alteration of the articles) as authority for those profits to be so applied after that date.
@ref s 848(1) Saving for certain older provisions in articles (src:11393-11393)
GIVEN `immediately before the relevant date the company was authorised by a provision of its articles to apply its unrealised profits in paying up in full or in part unissued shares to be allotted to members of the company as fully or partly paid bonus shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision has been altered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 848(1) that provision continues as authority for those profits to be so applied after the relevant date` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `immediately before the relevant date the company was authorised by a provision of its articles to apply its unrealised profits in paying up in full or in part unissued shares to be allotted to members of the company as fully or partly paid bonus shares`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where immediately before the relevant date a company was authorised by a provision of its articles to apply its unrealised profits in paying up ... that provision continues"
        IF `the provision has been altered` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "that provision continues (subject to any alteration of the articles)": what an altered provision authorises depends on the alteration
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 849 Restriction on application of unrealised profits`

-- src:11397 | 849 Restriction on application of unrealised profits
-- src:11398 | A company must not apply an unrealised profit in paying up debentures or any amounts unpaid on its issued shares.
@ref s 849 Restriction on application of unrealised profits (src:11397-11398)
GIVEN `the profit is an unrealised profit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 849 the company may apply the profit in paying up debentures or any amounts unpaid on its issued shares` MEANS
    IF `the profit is an unrealised profit`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company must not apply an unrealised profit in paying up debentures or any amounts unpaid on its issued shares."
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A company must not apply an unrealised profit": a realised profit is not mentioned

@ref s 849 Restriction on application of unrealised profits (src:11397-11398)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Action of a party`
`s 849 the company must not apply an unrealised profit in paying up debentures or amounts unpaid on its issued shares` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    SHANT (`Action of a party` OF Company, Company, "s 849 applies an unrealised profit in paying up debentures or amounts unpaid on its issued shares")
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "s 849: an unrealised profit was applied in paying up debentures or amounts unpaid on issued shares"

§§ `s 850 Treatment of certain older profits or losses`

-- src:11402 | (3) For the purposes of this section the relevant date is—
-- src:11403 | (a) for companies registered in Great Britain, 22nd December 1980;
-- src:11404 | (b) for companies registered in Northern Ireland, 1st July 1983.
@ref s 850(3) Treatment of certain older profits or losses (src:11402-11404)
GIVEN `the place where the company is registered` IS A `Place of registration`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 850(3) the relevant date for a company registered in the place` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the place where the company is registered`
    WHEN `England and Wales` THEN Date 22 12 1980
    WHEN `Scotland` THEN Date 22 12 1980
    WHEN `Northern Ireland` THEN Date 1 7 1983

-- src:11400 | (1) Where the directors of a company are, after making all reasonable enquiries, unable to determine whether a particular profit made before the relevant date is realised or unrealised, they may treat the profit as realised.
@ref s 850(1) Treatment of certain older profits or losses (src:11400-11400)
GIVEN `the place where the company is registered` IS A `Place of registration`
      `the date on which the profit was made` IS A DATE
      `the directors, after making all reasonable enquiries, are unable to determine whether the profit is realised or unrealised` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 850(1) the directors may treat the profit as realised` MEANS
    IF     `the directors, after making all reasonable enquiries, are unable to determine whether the profit is realised or unrealised`
       AND Day `the date on which the profit was made` LESS THAN Day (`s 850(3) the relevant date for a company registered in the place` `the place where the company is registered`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the directors of a company are, after making all reasonable enquiries, unable to determine whether a particular profit made before the relevant date is realised or unrealised, they may treat the profit as realised."

-- src:11401 | (2) Where the directors of a company, after making all reasonable enquiries, are unable to determine whether a particular loss made before the relevant date is realised or unrealised, they may treat the loss as unrealised.
@ref s 850(2) Treatment of certain older profits or losses (src:11401-11401)
GIVEN `the place where the company is registered` IS A `Place of registration`
      `the date on which the loss was made` IS A DATE
      `the directors, after making all reasonable enquiries, are unable to determine whether the loss is realised or unrealised` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 850(2) the directors may treat the loss as unrealised` MEANS
    IF     `the directors, after making all reasonable enquiries, are unable to determine whether the loss is realised or unrealised`
       AND Day `the date on which the loss was made` LESS THAN Day (`s 850(3) the relevant date for a company registered in the place` `the place where the company is registered`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the directors of a company, after making all reasonable enquiries, are unable to determine whether a particular loss made before the relevant date is realised or unrealised, they may treat the loss as unrealised."

§§ `s 851 Application of rules of law restricting distributions`

-- src:11406 | (1) Except as provided in this section, the provisions of this Part are without prejudice to any rule of law restricting the sums out of which, or the cases in which, a distribution may be made.
@ref s 851(1) Application of rules of law restricting distributions (src:11406-11406)
GIVEN `the restriction is imposed by a rule of law restricting the sums out of which, or the cases in which, a distribution may be made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter is provided for in section 851` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 851(1) the provisions of this Part are without prejudice to the rule of law` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the matter is provided for in section 851` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Except as provided in this section, the provisions of this Part are without prejudice to any rule of law" (an "except" met)
        IF `the restriction is imposed by a rule of law restricting the sums out of which, or the cases in which, a distribution may be made` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any rule of law restricting the sums out of which, or the cases in which, a distribution may be made"

-- src:11407 | (2) For the purposes of any rule of law requiring distributions to be paid out of profits or restricting the return of capital to members—
-- src:11408 | (a) section 845 (distributions in kind: determination of amount) applies to determine the amount of any distribution or return of capital consisting of or including, or treated as arising in consequence of the sale, transfer or other disposition by a company of a non-cash asset; and
-- src:11409 | (b) section 846 (distributions in kind: treatment of unrealised profits) applies as it applies for the purposes of this Part.
@ref s 851(2) Application of rules of law restricting distributions (src:11407-11409)
GIVEN `the rule of law requires distributions to be paid out of profits or restricts the return of capital to members` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the distribution or return of capital consists of or includes, or is treated as arising in consequence of, the sale, transfer or other disposition by a company of a non-cash asset` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 851(2)(a) section 845 applies to determine the amount of the distribution or return of capital` MEANS
    IF `the rule of law requires distributions to be paid out of profits or restricts the return of capital to members` AND `the distribution or return of capital consists of or includes, or is treated as arising in consequence of, the sale, transfer or other disposition by a company of a non-cash asset`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purposes of any rule of law requiring distributions to be paid out of profits or restricting the return of capital to members— (a) section 845 ... applies to determine the amount of any distribution or return of capital consisting of or including ... a non-cash asset"

@ref s 851(2)(b) Application of rules of law restricting distributions (src:11409-11409)
GIVEN `the rule of law requires distributions to be paid out of profits or restricts the return of capital to members` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 851(2)(b) section 846 applies as it applies for the purposes of this Part` MEANS
    IF `the rule of law requires distributions to be paid out of profits or restricts the return of capital to members`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purposes of any rule of law requiring distributions to be paid out of profits or restricting the return of capital to members— ... (b) section 846 ... applies as it applies for the purposes of this Part."

-- src:11410 | (3) In this section references to distributions are to amounts regarded as distributions for the purposes of any such rule of law as is referred to in subsection (1).
@ref s 851(3) Application of rules of law restricting distributions (src:11410-11410)
GIVEN `the reference is a reference in section 851 to distributions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 851(3) the reference is to amounts regarded as distributions for the purposes of the rule of law` MEANS
    IF `the reference is a reference in section 851 to distributions`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In this section references to distributions are to amounts regarded as distributions for the purposes of any such rule of law as is referred to in subsection (1)."

§§ `s 852 Saving for other restrictions on distributions`

-- src:11411 | 852 Saving for other restrictions on distributions
-- src:11412 | The provisions of this Part are without prejudice to any enactment, or any provision of a company's articles, restricting the sums out of which, or the cases in which, a distribution may be made.
