§§ `s 853 Minor definitions`

-- src:11415 | (2) References to profit or losses of any description—
-- src:11416 | (a) are to profits or losses of that description made at any time, and
-- src:11417 | (b) except where the context otherwise requires, are to profits or losses of a revenue or capital character.
@ref s 853(2) Minor definitions (src:11415-11417)
GIVEN `the profit or loss is of that description` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 853(2)(a) the profit or loss is within the reference, whenever it was made` MEANS
    IF `the profit or loss is of that description`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "References to profit or losses of any description— (a) are to profits or losses of that description made at any time"

@ref s 853(2)(b) Minor definitions (src:11417-11417)
GIVEN `the context otherwise requires` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the profit or loss is of a revenue or capital character` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 853(2)(b) the profit or loss is within the reference` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the context otherwise requires` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "except where the context otherwise requires"
        IF `the profit or loss is of a revenue or capital character` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "are to profits or losses of a revenue or capital character"

DECLARE `s 853(3) operation` IS ONE OF
    `s 853(3)(a) applying the profits in wholly or partly paying up unissued shares in the company to be allotted to members of the company as fully or partly paid bonus shares`
    `s 853(3)(b) transferring the profits to capital redemption reserve`
    `s 853(3) another operation`

-- src:11418 | (3) “Capitalisation”, in relation to a company's profits, means any of the following operations (whenever carried out)—
-- src:11419 | (a) applying the profits in wholly or partly paying up unissued shares in the company to be allotted to members of the company as fully or partly paid bonus shares, or
-- src:11420 | (b) transferring the profits to capital redemption reserve.
@ref s 853(3) Minor definitions (src:11418-11420)
GIVEN operation IS A `s 853(3) operation`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 853(3) the operation is capitalisation` MEANS
    CONSIDER operation
    WHEN `s 853(3)(a) applying the profits in wholly or partly paying up unissued shares in the company to be allotted to members of the company as fully or partly paid bonus shares` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 853(3)(b) transferring the profits to capital redemption reserve` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Capitalisation”, in relation to a company's profits, means any of the following operations (whenever carried out)"

-- src:11421 | (4) References to “realised profits” and “realised losses”, in relation to a company's accounts, are to such profits or losses of the company as fall to be treated as realised in accordance with principles generally accepted at the time when the accounts are prepared, with respect to the determination for accounting purposes of realised profits or losses.
@ref s 853(4) Minor definitions (src:11421-11421)
GIVEN `the profit or loss falls to be treated as realised in accordance with principles generally accepted at the time when the accounts are prepared, with respect to the determination for accounting purposes of realised profits or losses` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 853(4) the profit or loss is a realised profit or loss in relation to the company's accounts` MEANS
    IF `the profit or loss falls to be treated as realised in accordance with principles generally accepted at the time when the accounts are prepared, with respect to the determination for accounting purposes of realised profits or losses`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "References to “realised profits” and “realised losses”, in relation to a company's accounts, are to such profits or losses of the company as fall to be treated as realised in accordance with principles generally accepted at the time when the accounts are prepared"

-- src:11422 | (5) Subsection (4) is without prejudice to—
-- src:11423 | (a) the construction of any other expression (where appropriate) by reference to accepted accounting principles or practice, or
-- src:11424 | (b) any specific provision for the treatment of profits or losses of any description as realised.
@ref s 853(5) Minor definitions (src:11422-11424)
GIVEN `the matter is the construction of another expression by reference to accepted accounting principles or practice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter is a specific provision for the treatment of profits or losses of any description as realised` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 853(5) subsection (4) is without prejudice to the matter` MEANS
    IF `the matter is the construction of another expression by reference to accepted accounting principles or practice` OR `the matter is a specific provision for the treatment of profits or losses of any description as realised`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subsection (4) is without prejudice to— (a) the construction of any other expression ..., (b) any specific provision for the treatment of profits or losses of any description as realised."

-- src:11425 | (6) “Fixed assets” means assets of a company which are intended for use on a continuing basis in the company's activities.
@ref s 853(6) Minor definitions (src:11425-11425)
GIVEN `the asset is intended for use on a continuing basis in the company's activities` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 853(6) the asset is a fixed asset` MEANS
    IF `the asset is intended for use on a continuing basis in the company's activities`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Fixed assets” means assets of a company which are intended for use on a continuing basis in the company's activities."
